# Local configuration. Copy to `.env` and edit. The `.env` file is gitignored.
#
# `just` auto-loads variables from `.env` (see `set dotenv-load` in justfile).

# Absolute path to your local Slay the Spire 2 install directory.
# `just` reads this file via dotenv: values containing spaces must be
# wrapped in single or double quotes, and the quotes are stripped before
# the value is exported (so `"/foo bar"` becomes `/foo bar`). Do not use
# `~` or backslash-escape spaces — neither is expanded.
#
# Linux ships sts2.dll at the install root:
#   STS2_GAME_DIR="/home/<user>/.steam/steam/steamapps/common/Slay the Spire 2"
#   STS2_GAME_DIR="/home/<user>/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/common/Slay the Spire 2"
# Secondary Steam library:
#   STS2_GAME_DIR="/run/media/<user>/<disk>/SteamLibrary/steamapps/common/Slay the Spire 2"
# macOS hides the DLLs inside the .app bundle under
# `SlayTheSpire2.app/Contents/Resources/data_sts2_macos_<arch>/`; point
# STS2_GAME_DIR at the install root and `just pull-game-libs` will dig in:
#   STS2_GAME_DIR="/Users/<user>/Library/Application Support/Steam/steamapps/common/Slay the Spire 2"
STS2_GAME_DIR="/path/to/Slay the Spire 2"

# Temporary escape hatch (AD-3 amendment pending). Set to 1 to bypass the
# sts2.dll SHA-256 pin check in `just pull-game-libs`. The check is correct
# on Linux but currently rejects any macOS install because Godot's C#
# pipeline emits per-arch DLLs that don't match the Linux-recorded pin.
# Remove this once a per-platform pin lands.
# STS2_SKIP_SHA_CHECK=1

# ── Private vendor mirror ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed when running without a local Steam install (CI's trusted
# tier, ephemeral Claude containers, or a maintainer pushing a new pin).
# Local development uses STS2_GAME_DIR above and ignores these.
#
# The mirror holds the same 10 DLLs as vendor/, encrypted with age. Three
# secrets, each with its own role:
#
#   STS2_VENDOR_REPO     — owner/repo of the private mirror.
#   STS2_VENDOR_TOKEN    — fine-grained PAT scoped only to that repo.
#                          Read scope is enough to fetch; write scope is
#                          needed to push (just setup::push-vendor).
#   STS2_VENDOR_PUBKEY   — age recipient (public key). Not secret;
#                          anyone with it can only encrypt. Used by
#                          push-vendor.
#   STS2_VENDOR_PRIVKEY  — age identity (private key). The decryption
#                          secret. Required by fetch-vendor. Treat like
#                          a password — never check in, never paste in
#                          chat.
#   STS2_VENDOR_REF      — optional; mirror branch (default: main).
#
# One-time keypair generation: `age-keygen` prints both keys. Copy the
# "public key:" comment value into STS2_VENDOR_PUBKEY and the full
# AGE-SECRET-KEY-1… line into STS2_VENDOR_PRIVKEY.
#
# STS2_VENDOR_REPO="julians/headless-in-the-spire-vendor"
# STS2_VENDOR_TOKEN="github_pat_..."
# STS2_VENDOR_PUBKEY="age1..."
# STS2_VENDOR_PRIVKEY="AGE-SECRET-KEY-1..."
# STS2_VENDOR_REF="main"
